OL,3,AGerman Chancellor Merz vows to stay on
OL,4,Adespite 'disaster' in state election
OL,5,
OL,6,FEmbattled German Chancellor Friedrich
OL,7,FMerz has vowed to stay on despite exit
OL,8,Fpolls in two local elections suggesting
OL,9,Fdamaging defeats for his centre-right
OL,10,FChristian Democratic Union (CDU) party.
OL,12,FIn the north-eastern state of
OL,13,FMecklenburg-Vorpommern, the party was
OL,14,Fprojected to only just scrape into
OL,15,Fparliament, while the AfD was on track
OL,16,Fto win the most votes. Merz called the
OL,17,Fresult "a disaster" for his party.
OL,19,FIn Berlin, the ruling CDU was also
OL,20,Fexpected to be beaten by Die Linke (The
OL,21,FLeft).
OL,23,APub: 20-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
